  "notes": "Sarawak Oil Palms Berhad (SOP) \u2014 Bursa Malaysia stock code 5126, listed on the Main Board (then KLSE) since 25 April 1991. Sarawak-state-focused integrated oil palm producer combining upstream estates (~85,000-94,000 ha planted across Miri, Bintulu, Kanowit and Mukah divisions in Sarawak) with downstream refinery, kernel-crushing plant and biodiesel facility at Bintulu. December 31 fiscal year-end; quarterly Form 8 reports filed with Bursa. Reported segments: Plantation (FFB / CPO / PK), Manufacturing (refining, kernel crushing, biodiesel), and Investment Holding / Others. Quarterly revenue, segment revenue, PBT, net profit, EPS, DPS sourced from Bursa Form 8 filings and KLSE Screener historical mirror; EBITDA estimated as PBT + finance cost + D&A. Annual history extended to FY2000 from successive SOP annual reports' five-year financial highlights tables \u2014 pre-2008 numbers reflect pre-bonus-issue share base (~285M shares); 2008 1:1 bonus issue lifted shares to ~571M (rounded). Per-period totalAcresK reflects approximate planted oil palm hectares \u00d7 2.471 \u2192 acres. NAV/share = total equity attributable to owners \u00f7 shares outstanding. FY24 latest reconciles to seed comps: revenue ~RM 5.67B, EBITDA ~RM 784M, NAV/share ~RM 5.03, planted ~190K acres.",
